I deployed my Azure AI Text Analyzer web application to Azure Container Apps in the Sweden Central region. The app is a Flask application served by Gunicorn, and it runs as a container from my public Docker Hub image prikuh/azure-ai-text-analyzer. It uses the Azure AI Language service for sentiment analysis, key phrases and entity recognition.

The infrastructure is defined with Terraform: a resource group, a Log Analytics workspace, a free tier Language service, a Container Apps environment, the Container App itself and the role assignment. The Terraform state is stored in Azure Storage. The app has no keys or secrets: it calls the Language service with the managed identity of the Container App, which has a least-privilege role on the service. The code is in https://github.com/priku/ai-test-azure.

The app scales to zero when idle to keep the costs low, so the first request after a pause can take about 20 seconds.
